{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Learning Rate Schedules and Warmup Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Schedule Functions"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Each function takes the current step and returns the learning rate at that step."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import math"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def constant_schedule(step, lr=0.01, **kwargs):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return lr"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def step_decay_schedule(step, lr=0.1, step_size=100, gamma=0.1, **kwargs):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return lr * (gamma ** (step // step_size))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def cosine_schedule(step, lr=0.01, total_steps=1000, lr_min=1e-5, **kwargs):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if step >= total_steps:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return lr_min"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return lr_min + 0.5 * (lr - lr_min) * (1 + math.cos(math.pi * step / total_steps))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def warmup_cosine_schedule(step, lr=0.01, total_steps=1000, warmup_steps=100, lr_min=1e-5, **kwargs):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if total_steps <= warmup_steps:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return lr * (step / max(warmup_steps, 1))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if step < warmup_steps:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return lr * step / warmup_steps"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    progress = (step - warmup_steps) / (total_steps - warmup_steps)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return lr_min + 0.5 * (lr - lr_min) * (1 + math.cos(math.pi * progress))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def one_cycle_schedule(step, lr=0.01, total_steps=1000, **kwargs):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    mid = max(total_steps // 2, 1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if step < mid:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return (lr / 25) + (lr - lr / 25) * step / mid"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        progress = (step - mid) / max(total_steps - mid, 1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return lr * (1 - progress) + (lr / 10000) * progress"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Visualize All Schedules"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Print a text-based plot showing how each schedule evolves over training."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def visualize_schedule(name, schedule_fn, total_steps=500, **kwargs):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    steps = list(range(0, total_steps, total_steps // 20))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if total_steps - 1 not in steps:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        steps.append(total_steps - 1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    lrs = [schedule_fn(s, total_steps=total_steps, **kwargs) for s in steps]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    max_lr = max(lrs) if max(lrs) > 0 else 1.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"\\n{name}:\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for s, lr_val in zip(steps, lrs):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        bar_len = int(lr_val / max_lr * 40)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        bar = \"#\" * bar_len"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        print(f\"  Step {s:4d}: lr={lr_val:.6f} {bar}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Training Network"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "A simple two-layer network on the circle dataset, same as previous lessons, but now we vary the schedule."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import random"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def sigmoid(x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x = max(-500, min(500, x))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return 1.0 / (1.0 + math.exp(-x))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def relu(x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return max(0.0, x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def relu_deriv(x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return 1.0 if x > 0 else 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def make_circle_data(n=200, seed=42):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    random.seed(seed)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    data = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for _ in range(n):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = random.uniform(-2, 2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        y = random.uniform(-2, 2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        label = 1.0 if x * x + y * y < 1.5 else 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        data.append(([x, y], label))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return data"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def train_with_schedule(schedule_fn, schedule_name, data, epochs=300, base_lr=0.05, **kwargs):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    random.seed(0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    hidden_size = 8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    total_steps = epochs * len(data)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    std = math.sqrt(2.0 / 2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    w1 = [[random.gauss(0, std) for _ in range(2)] for _ in range(hidden_size)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    b1 = [0.0] * hidden_size"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    w2 = [random.gauss(0, std) for _ in range(hidden_size)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    b2 = 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    step = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    epoch_losses = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for epoch in range(epochs):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        total_loss = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        correct = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for x, target in data:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            lr = schedule_fn(step, lr=base_lr, total_steps=total_steps, **kwargs)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            z1 = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            h = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for i in range(hidden_size):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                z = w1[i][0] * x[0] + w1[i][1] * x[1] + b1[i]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                z1.append(z)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                h.append(relu(z))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            z2 = sum(w2[i] * h[i] for i in range(hidden_size)) + b2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            out = sigmoid(z2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            error = out - target"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            d_out = error * out * (1 - out)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for i in range(hidden_size):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                d_h = d_out * w2[i] * relu_deriv(z1[i])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                w2[i] -= lr * d_out * h[i]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                for j in range(2):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    w1[i][j] -= lr * d_h * x[j]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                b1[i] -= lr * d_h"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            b2 -= lr * d_out"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            total_loss += (out - target) ** 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if (out >= 0.5) == (target >= 0.5):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                correct += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            step += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        avg_loss = total_loss / len(data)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        accuracy = correct / len(data) * 100"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        epoch_losses.append(avg_loss)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return epoch_losses"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Compare All Schedules"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Train the same network with each schedule and compare final loss and convergence behavior."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def compare_schedules(data):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    configs = ["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        (\"Constant\", constant_schedule, {}),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        (\"Step Decay\", step_decay_schedule, {\"step_size\": 15000, \"gamma\": 0.1}),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        (\"Cosine\", cosine_schedule, {\"lr_min\": 1e-5}),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        (\"Warmup+Cosine\", warmup_cosine_schedule, {\"warmup_steps\": 3000, \"lr_min\": 1e-5}),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        (\"1cycle\", one_cycle_schedule, {}),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"\\n{'Schedule':<20} {'Start Loss':>12} {'Mid Loss':>12} {'End Loss':>12} {'Best Loss':>12}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(\"-\" * 70)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for name, schedule_fn, extra_kwargs in configs:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        losses = train_with_schedule(schedule_fn, name, data, epochs=300, base_lr=0.05, **extra_kwargs)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        mid_idx = len(losses) // 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        best = min(losses)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        print(f\"{name:<20} {losses[0]:>12.6f} {losses[mid_idx]:>12.6f} {losses[-1]:>12.6f} {best:>12.6f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: LR Too High vs Too Low"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Demonstrate the three failure modes: too high (divergence), too low (crawling), and just right."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def lr_sensitivity(data):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    learning_rates = [1.0, 0.1, 0.01, 0.001, 0.0001]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(\"\\nLR Sensitivity (constant schedule, 100 epochs):\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"  {'LR':>10} {'Start Loss':>12} {'End Loss':>12} {'Status':>15}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(\"  \" + \"-\" * 52)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for lr in learning_rates:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        losses = train_with_schedule(constant_schedule, f\"lr={lr}\", data, epochs=100, base_lr=lr)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        start = losses[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        end = losses[-1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if end > start or math.isnan(end) or end > 1.0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            status = \"DIVERGED\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        elif end > start * 0.9:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            status = \"BARELY MOVED\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        elif end < 0.15:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            status = \"CONVERGED\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            status = \"LEARNING\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        end_str = f\"{end:.6f}\" if not math.isnan(end) else \"NaN\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        print(f\"  {lr:>10.4f} {start:>12.6f} {end_str:>12} {status:>15}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Implement exponential decay: lr(t) = lr_0 * gamma^t where gamma = 0.999. Compare to cosine annealing on the circle dataset.\n\n2. Implement the learning rate range test (Leslie Smith): train for a few hundred steps while exponentially increasing the LR from 1e-7 to 1. Plot loss vs LR. The optimal max LR is just before the loss starts increasing.\n\n3. Train with warmup + cosine but vary the warmup length: 0%, 1%, 5%, 10%, 20% of total steps. Find the sweet spot where training is most stable.\n\n4. Implement cosine annealing with warm restarts (SGDR): reset the learning rate to lr_max every T steps and decay again. Compare to standard cosine on a longer training run.\n\n5. Build a \"schedule surgeon\" that monitors training loss and automatically switches from warmup to cosine when the loss stabilizes, and reduces lr if the loss plateaus for too long."
      ]
    }
  ],
